WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.650
- Well, welcome to another
episode of the "Addy Hour",

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.860
it's been my pleasure to
continue to engage with you on

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.760
these conversations.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.740
And today I'm really excited
to welcome two special guests

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.080
to the program to talk about
a really important topic.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.620
Our first guest is Stacey D. Stewart,

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.650
and Stacey is the president
and CEO of the March of Dimes,

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.250
where she has been in
that role since 2017.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.610
And she heads the organization
that really is leading the

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.660
fight for the health of moms and babies.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.170
Prior to joining the March of Dimes,

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.090
she was actually the
president of the United Way,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.840
the nation's largest
nonprofit organization

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.195
and served in that role even
prior to being president in

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:43.574
that organization was also
the executive vice president

00:00:43.574 --> 00:00:46.370
of community impact
leadership and learning,

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.000
where she developed global partnerships

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.030
to advance community impact
in more than 40 countries.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.960
So definitely a person who
has had a lot of impact,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.090
in a lot of ways.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.970
She's had, she's a business veteran,

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.190
who's had a lot of different senior roles,

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.340
has a background in finance
and investment banking

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.830
and continues to serve on lots
of different national boards

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.750
and in the Washington
DC metropolitan area.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.583
So I'm thrilled, excited,

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:09.800
and honored to welcome Stacey
Stewart to the program today.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:10.890
Thanks for being here.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.570
- Thanks for having me.
It's a pleasure to be here.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.995
- Definitely looking
forward to the conversation.

00:01:15.995 --> 00:01:19.420
Our next guest is Angelina Spicer.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.150
Angelina is a comedian
social media influencer

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.895
and accidental activist.

00:01:23.895 --> 00:01:26.279
A cum laude graduate of Howard,

00:01:26.279 --> 00:01:30.240
Angelina is known for her
deep and authentic comedy.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.890
She's had just outstanding
success has been her videos

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.770
and her content has been viewed
more than 90 million times

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.653
in more than 45 countries.

00:01:39.653 --> 00:01:42.730
She was a regular sketch
performer on "Jimmy Kimmel Live"

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.590
and then "Conan" has
also appeared on "Ellen"

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.540
and "On The Real".

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:50.639
In 2017, Angelina also
became an outspoken advocate

00:01:50.639 --> 00:01:54.070
for maternal mental health,
after her own diagnosis

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.720
and hospitalization with
postpartum depression.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:57.620
But in addition to that,

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.280
she's also been working
with lawmakers in California

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.600
and on Capitol Hill to
implement laws to support

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.970
early maternal health,

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.550
has worked with lots of
different organizations,

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.550
including Cedars-Sinai hospital,

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.050
Postpartum Support International,

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.510
the World Health Organization, and others,

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.500
and is currently in production
on "The Push for Permission"

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.835
a feature length
documentary that uses comedy

00:02:17.835 --> 00:02:20.760
to empower women, to
advocate for themselves

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.260
and to normalize postpartum depression.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.690
So I'm grateful and
honored to welcome Angelina

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.910
to the program today as well.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.170
Thanks for being here.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.723
- Thank you for having me!

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:33.815
- Of course, my pleasure.

00:02:33.815 --> 00:02:36.040
And as we talked offline
before I even started,

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.355
my goal today is to see if I
can keep up with the energy,

00:02:38.355 --> 00:02:41.720
in the room, so to speak.
(all laughing)

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.890
I'm really excited and honored though.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.240
But I've been really
looking forward to this

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.268
for several different reasons,

00:02:46.268 --> 00:02:48.510
which I've alluded to already;

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.280
one, just because of the
impact and the influence

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.480
that both of you had, have as
a black women in our society.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.313
I think that's so important,

00:02:56.313 --> 00:02:58.150
it's so important for us to elevate

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.948
and to continue to amplify
and just the important topics

00:03:00.948 --> 00:03:02.746
that you've both been talking about

00:03:02.746 --> 00:03:05.290
and the impact you've
had policy-wise as well.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.278
I think that's really impressive.

00:03:07.278 --> 00:03:10.030
The other piece that I think
we'll get to as we go through

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.800
